{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Her heads</b> — they are the heads of Jerusalem; they are the kings." "<b>For bribe they judge, and her priests for a price</b> — that they take." "<b>And her prophets</b> — they are the false prophets, because of silver that they give them. <b>They divine</b> — and the word קסם in Ishmaelite is like 'cutting,' as though saying: thus it will be, and near to it is גוזרים. And behold, a diviner of divinations is a comprehensive name for the arts mentioned afterward." "And the meaning of <b>Is not HaShem in our midst</b> is like 'The temple of YHWH, the temple of YHWH.'"], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:50.275755288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}